\par\b\fs28 A2. Connecting hypotheses\b0\fs24\par


\par Hypothesis 1 (one axis): the centre is Source alone \u8212? all is gift, and the human receives. The response stays in the background.\par


\par Hypothesis 2 (relation): the centre is the relation Source \u8596? Will \u8212? God remembers, hears and gives, and therefore the human is waked and called to hear, to receive and to give back.\par


\par Which explains the most data with the least strain? Hypothesis 2. It explains why the day is called teruah (an imperative, not mere gift), why Hannah makes a vow and gives back, and why Matthew 24 runs out to \u8220?watch.\u8221? Hypothesis 1 leaves teruah and the giving-back unexplained.\par


\par What would refute this reading? If teruah were pure comfort and Hannah's song a sweet thank-you, the weight would lie with Source alone.\par



