\par\b\fs28 A4. Movement\b0\fs24\par


\par What is unmasked? The anxious holding-on as though we had made it \u8212? and the subtle variant \u8220?God needs my help\u8221? (Ishmael), where we still believe the promise but seize the process.\par


\par What frame does the text put in its place? The God who remembers, hears and gives \u8212? and who wakes us with a sound: receive as gift, and give back into His service.\par


\par What concrete response and formation follow? Truly hearing instead of growing used to it; giving back as a wakeful act (Hannah); and watching with open hands, even without knowing the hour (Matt. 24).\par


\par \b Core sentence:\b0  The sound wakes us \u8212? receive what is entrusted to you, and lay it open in the hand of the One who hears and remembers.\par


\par \b Horizon (ground, not the week's theme):\b0  the last trumpet (Matt. 24:31) \u8212? the same God who remembered Sarah and Hannah calls His children together at the end.\par


